    Because the two files mix the years of (a) and (b), and because the
    licence of (a) can be withdrawn and requires an indemnity, which the
    MIT licence of qesR cannot pass on, these two files, and the validation
    report computed from them (below), are excluded from the package build;
    they are used only in the source repository (its tests,
    data-raw/build_validation.R and the website) and are not covered by
    the MIT licence.
  - inst/extdata/validation/census_margins.csv: counts of the Quebec
    population by gender, age group, mother tongue and highest certificate
    at the censuses of 2006, 2011 (education from the 2011 National
    Household Survey), 2016 and 2021, summed from Statistics Canada tables
    98-10-0020-01, 98-10-0218-01 and 98-10-0384-01, the 2011 Census Profile
    (catalogue 98-316-XWE2011001) and the 2006 Census topic-based table
    97-551-XCB2006009 (each row gives its table and URL; the 2006 table is
    no longer on Statistics Canada's site, and its Beyond 20/20 file was
    retrieved from the Internet Archive's capture of Statistics Canada's
    download link), used under the Statistics Canada Open Licence
    (https://www.statcan.gc.ca/en/terms-conditions/open-licence). The sums
    and shares are qesR's. Adapted from Statistics Canada, Census of
